<h2 id="introduction">Introduction <a id="sec-intro"></a></h2>
<p>This is a basic example. The section uses a target label. The next section (Sec. ref:sec-citations uses a <code>CUSTOM_ID</code>).</p>
<h3 id="sec-citations">Citations</h3>
<p>index:citations</p>
<p>Here are a few typical</p>
<dl>
<dt>cite</dt>
<dd><a href=""></a></dd>
<dt>citeauthor</dt>
<dd><a href=""></a></dd>
<dt>citenum</dt>
<dd><a href=""></a></dd>
</dl>
<p>index:label!table</p>












<table id="tab-data"><caption>some tabular data.</caption><tbody><tr><td>x</td><td>y</td></tr><tr><td>0</td><td>1</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>index:label!figure</p>
<figure id="fig-cos">
<img src="./fig.png" alt="fig.png">
<figcaption>You need a caption.</figcaption>
</figure>
<p>Here is an equation using a latex label inside it.:</p>
<p>
∫_0^1 e^x dx
</p>
<h3 id="cross-references">cross-references <a id="sec-cr"></a></h3>
<p>index:cross-references</p>
<p>See section ref:sec-intro. The data is shown in Table ref:tab-data.</p>
<p>Here are some alternate kinds of refs.</p>
<dl>
<dt>page</dt>
<dd>Fig. ref:fig-cos is on page  pageref:fig-cos</dd>
<dt>name</dt>
<dd>nameref:fig-cos (uses the caption)</dd>
<dt>equation</dt>
<dd>Eq. eqref:eq-int</dd>
</dl>
<p>If you use <a href="https://ctan.org/pkg/cleveref?lang=en">cleveref</a>, these cross-references will be modified at compile time so they have a descriptor in front of each label:</p>
<ul>
<li>cref:sec-intro</li>
<li>cref:tab-data</li>
<li>cref:fig-cos</li>
<li>cref:eq-int</li>
</ul>
<p>These are capitalized versions.</p>
<ul>
<li>Cref:sec-intro</li>
<li>Cref:tab-data</li>
<li>Cref:fig-cos</li>
<li>Cref:eq-int</li>
</ul>
<p>You can also put several together  Cref:sec-intro,tab-data,fig-cos,eq-int</p>
<p>And for numerically sequential sequences, they will be collapsed when compiled to a range: cref:sec-cr,sec-misc,sec-citations. How this is done is customized in LaTeX, see the <code>cleveref</code> documentation.</p>
